WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.083
(enchanting bell music)

00:00:01.083 --> 00:00:03.194
- [Narrator] This is the Addra Gazelle.

00:00:03.194 --> 00:00:07.361
This gorgeous gazelle is sadly
on the verge of extinction.

00:00:08.278 --> 00:00:11.035
Once spread across the
Sahara desert it is now only

00:00:11.035 --> 00:00:14.801
found in pockets of Chad, Mali, and Niger.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:17.455
Addra's are considered the
largest type of gazelle

00:00:17.455 --> 00:00:19.677
with very long legs.

00:00:19.677 --> 00:00:21.429
They're built lean and slender

00:00:21.429 --> 00:00:23.692
to survive the dessert heat.

00:00:23.692 --> 00:00:25.344
They're tan and brown coats blend

00:00:25.344 --> 00:00:27.333
with their native surroundings.

00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:31.038
They travel in herds; together
they browse and graze

00:00:31.038 --> 00:00:33.017
grass and leaves.

00:00:33.017 --> 00:00:35.852
Their strength in numbers
is a survival tactic

00:00:35.852 --> 00:00:38.712
as they count lions, leopards and cheetahs

00:00:38.712 --> 00:00:40.722
as their predators.

00:00:40.722 --> 00:00:43.369
In the last decade their
population has decreased

00:00:43.369 --> 00:00:45.473
by over 80%.

00:00:45.473 --> 00:00:49.162
Along with habitat destruction
poaching and overhunting

00:00:49.162 --> 00:00:51.508
for horns and meat have
caused the Addra to become

00:00:51.508 --> 00:00:53.352
critically endangered.

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:56.550
And some estimate their
numbers at less than 300

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.550
in the wild.

00:00:59.549 --> 00:01:01.716
This is the Addra Gazelle.

